<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  mutation-sweep: finish the corpus mutation baseline overnight.

  TEMPORARY, NOT PART OF THE STANDING SET. This is deliberately absent from install.sh's
  PLISTS array so a routine `install.sh` never resurrects it. As of 2026-09-01 it drives
  the FROM-SCRATCH re-sweep of all 108 auditable tools (10,811 mutants) that the
  2026-08-31 PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE fix made necessary - every pre-fix number may be a
  false kill.

  RE-ARMED 2026-09-08 for a FULL-CORPUS run: targets rebuilt to 138 selected / 134 auditable
  / 12,918 mutants / 0 engine errors. Wired hooks ARE measured here and that is deliberate:
  mutation_sweep skips them only when CLAUDECODE is set, which launchd does not set, so an
  unattended run covers all 134 including the 34 guards. A run started from inside a Claude
  session skips those 34 instead, because mutating a live guard makes that session's own tool
  calls answer to the mutant (measured 2026-09-07).

  ~12,918 mutants at the 2026-08 rate is well past one night. That is fine and expected: the
  sweep resumes by tool name against baseline.jsonl, so it picks up where it stopped. Unload it once the sweep reports SWEEP COMPLETE:
      launchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.nickmagnuson.jobsearch.mutation-sweep.plist
      rm ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.nickmagnuson.jobsearch.mutation-sweep.plist

  22:00, Nick's instruction 2026-09-13. HOUR HISTORY, so nobody "restores" a stale value:
  16:00 originally, 18:00 on 2026-09-01, 22:00 now. A 2026-09-08 correction found the prose
  and StartCalendarInterval disagreeing (prose 18:00, key 22) and settled both on 18. This
  change moves both to 22 deliberately. THE HOUR LIVES IN TWO PLACES IN THIS FILE, here and
  in StartCalendarInterval below. If you change one, change the other.

  WHY LATE. While this runs, one tools/*.py is mutated on disk at any instant and the tree is
  unsafe for ordinary work: tests/conftest.py refuses to run, and skills that shell out to
  tools/*.py would execute a mutant against real data. A 16:00 start put that inside a working
  afternoon. 22:00 is clear of the whole day.

  KNOWN TRADE AT 22:00, accepted. The run is long (~10h at the 2026-08 rate) and it quiesces 9
  launchd jobs for its duration, gmail-fetch and gmail-fetch-personal among them. From 18:00 it
  finished around 04:41 and the jobs were back before morning. From 22:00 a full run can still
  be going at 08:00, so /standup may report a stale Gmail fetch and see quiesced jobs. That is
  the sweep working, not a fault. The sweep restores every job on exit, including on SIGTERM.
  Check tools/launchd/logs/mutation-sweep.log for "restored 9 launchd job(s)" before treating a
  stalled fetch as broken.

  IT RECURS UNTIL UNLOADED, AND THAT IS SAFE. mutation_sweep resumes by tool name against
  baseline.jsonl, so a second 22:00 fire finds 0 unbanked tools and exits in seconds. The
  cost of forgetting is noise in the log, not a re-run.

  CAFFEINATE. The run is ~7 hours. Without -is the Mac idle-sleeps partway and the sweep
  is suspended mid-tool, which strands a .mutation_backup and makes the next run refuse
  at conftest. -i blocks idle sleep, -s blocks system sleep while on AC power.

  LOG FILES: never create, touch, or truncate anything in tools/launchd/logs/ from a Claude
  Code Bash call - files created that way inherit a com.apple.provenance xattr that launchd
  cannot open, and the job dies at EX_CONFIG (78) before the script runs, logging nothing.
  Rotation must DELETE and let launchd recreate. See reference_launchd_ex_config_provenance_xattr.
  PATH IS SET INSIDE THE COMMAND, NOT IN EnvironmentVariables (2026-09-13). launchd's PATH
  puts /opt/homebrew/bin LAST, so a bare `python3` resolved to /usr/bin/python3, macOS system
  Python 3.9.6, while tools/*.py require 3.10+ (CLAUDE.md). The sweep itself names the
  interpreter absolutely and was fine; the damage was one level down. Its mapped test
  tests/scripts/test_no_silent_failures.py::test_a_representative_hook_runs_end_to_end executes a
  wired hook verbatim as `PYTHONIOENCODING=utf-8 python3 "$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/tools/check_public_pii.py"`,
  which died on 3.9 at check_public_pii.py:395 (`Path | None`, PEP 604, needs 3.10+) with
  "TypeError: unsupported operand type(s) for |". The baseline runs with -x, so that one failure
  aborted it and mutation_check reported `baseline_red`, whose message says "mapped tests fail on
  unmutated source" and names neither the test nor the interpreter. 19 of the 20 tools stuck that
  way map that test file. Six nights, 124 duplicate error rows, zero measurement banked.

  EnvironmentVariables would NOT fix it: ProgramArguments runs `bash -lc`, the login shell sources a
  profile that rebuilds PATH via path_helper, and that overwrites anything launchd injected. Setting
  it inside the command runs after the profile, so it wins.

  NOTE FOR EDITORS: this is an XML comment, so the two hyphen sequence is ILLEGAL anywhere inside
  it. `plutil -lint` and `launchctl load` both ACCEPT a plist containing one; python's plistlib
  rejects it, and plistlib is what tests/scripts/test_no_silent_failures.py uses. Verify any edit
  here with plistlib, not plutil.

  THIS IS THE NARROW FIX. The source defect is that hooks are wired with a bare `python3` in
  .claude/settings.json, so 54 of 141 tools crash under any system python first PATH, including
  check_public_pii.py and prepush_pii_guard.py, both PII gates, which fail OPEN because a crash
  exits 1 and only exit 2 blocks. Full context and fix options:
  output/analysis/091326-mutation-sweep-path-root-cause.md
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.nickmagnuson.jobsearch.mutation-sweep</string>
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/bash</string>
        <string>-lc</string>
        <string>export PATH="/opt/homebrew/bin:$PATH" &amp;&amp; cd "$HOME/Documents/Obsidian/30-projects/job-search" &amp;&amp; PYTHONIOENCODING=utf-8 /usr/bin/caffeinate -is /opt/homebrew/bin/python3 tools/mutation_sweep.py</string>
    </array>
    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <dict>
        <key>Hour</key><integer>22</integer>
        <key>Minute</key><integer>0</integer>
    </dict>
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/mag/Documents/Obsidian/30-projects/job-search/tools/launchd/logs/mutation-sweep.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/mag/Documents/Obsidian/30-projects/job-search/tools/launchd/logs/mutation-sweep.err</string>
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>
</dict>
</plist>
